Licence history
---------------

Transcripts was carved out of Scribe under MIT on 15 August 2026, went
proprietary ninety minutes later, and returned to MIT on 21 August 2026. The
grant is retroactive: LICENSE has been rewritten across the whole history, so
the forty-eight commits made inside that proprietary window carry the same terms
as the commits on either side of it, and a checkout of any commit gets the
licence that actually applies to it.

This is recorded because the rewrite left no trace of itself in git. Anyone
holding a copy taken during that window — or auditing the history and finding
the dates do not line up — is covered by the same MIT grant as everyone else.

The iOS app has no third-party dependencies. The list below applies to the
macOS build only.

